  "conclusions": [
    "Both aggregate SELECTs use idx_trips_org_id_pickup_time. Recent activity uses idx_trips_org_updated_at. No new trip index is justified by these samples.",
    "Isolated exact pg_timezone_names validation takes 787.874ms and explains the dominant wrapper overhead. The native timezone parser takes 1.472ms for the same canonical timezone but accepts a broader input grammar, so it is not a semantics-preserving replacement by itself.",
    "All measured plan root shared-read and temporary block counts are zero. No disk-read or sort-spill bottleneck appears in these samples.",
    "The organization_memberships sequential scan examines only 15 rows once in each visible aggregate/recent plan; existing org/user indexes are present. This does not justify adding a duplicate index."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One sample per query under one admin identity and one primary organization; not a cold-cache benchmark, load test, or driver/restricted-role validation.",
    "Aggregate ranges contain 45 and 17 visible trips. Existing model tests cover larger counts; these live samples do not demonstrate large-tenant scaling.",
    "Function Scan hides PL/pgSQL nested statements. The exact inner aggregate was profiled separately under the same claims, role and range; cache and plan-initialization conditions can differ.",
    "SQL execution timings exclude browser/PostgREST/auth/network transfer. CLI Management API wall time is deliberately excluded.",
    "Supabase plugin access remains unavailable for this project, but the verified linked CLI route succeeded. Docker/local DB was not used."
  ],
